WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.130
Change analysis compares observations across time.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.740
Before-and-after imagery can support construction tracking, damage assessment,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.595
environmental review, route status, and event timelines.

00:00:09.595 --> 00:00:13.190
The images must be comparable enough that collection differences are not mistaken for

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:13.935
scene changes.

00:00:13.935 --> 00:00:18.475
Repeat flights or observations should use consistent location, angle, altitude, lens,

00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:19.846
orientation, and coverage where safe and lawful.

00:00:19.846 --> 00:00:24.890
Record deviations because a shifted viewpoint can reveal or hide features and alter

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:25.850
apparent size.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.265
Seasonal differences matter.

00:00:27.265 --> 00:00:31.065
Leaf cover, snow, water level, crop state, and ground color may change normally.

00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:33.630
Lighting and shadow direction vary with time and weather.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.740
These effects can resemble damage, removal, or new objects.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.660
For construction or damage assessment, define measurable features before comparison.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.690
Record visible additions, removals, displacement, surface change, access change,

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.220
or debris.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.700
Avoid assigning cause or severity beyond what the imagery supports.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.100
Preserve event chronology.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.715
Distinguish capture time, file time, upload time, processing time, and report time.

00:00:54.715 --> 00:00:57.285
Metadata can help but may be missing or incorrect,

00:00:57.285 --> 00:01:00.115
so corroborate important timing with flight logs and other records.

00:01:00.115 --> 00:01:03.095
A useful comparison explains what changed, what remained stable,

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:06.510
how collection conditions differed, and how confident the judgment is.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:10.320
It also states what ground inspection or independent evidence is needed.
